--
Itanium C++ ABI 2.5.3 non-virtual thunks: the `this' adjustment is the base
subobject's offset in the laid-out class (with base-alignment padding).  The
thunk body was built when the overrider was declared, before add_padding ran,
with the unpadded offset (12 instead of 16 here); it is now rebuilt after the
layout (finalize_virtual_thunks).  Before: T::m read t and q from the wrong
addresses (pointer-outside-object-bounds and assertion failures).
The expected sizes and offsets are those of the LP64 x86_64 data model
(`--64'); the test is not meaningful in a 32-bit configuration.
